# The build context. Two things matter here, and only one of them is speed.
#
# `node_modules` is the correctness one: the Dockerfile runs `npm ci` to install
# the *Linux* native binaries (see DEPLOY.md §6) and then `COPY . .`. Without
# this file that COPY drops the host's macOS binaries on top of them, and the
# image either fails to build or ships @rolldown/binding-darwin-arm64 to a
# Linux container.
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
.git
.github
*.log
.vite
.eslintcache

# The SQLite file and its sidecars. The database belongs on the mounted volume
# at /data, never baked into an image layer.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
server/data

# Env files at every level, not just the root — `.env` alone would not match
# `server/.env.local`, which will hold the Resend API key. They must never reach
# the image: secrets come from Railway at runtime, and a stray `app/.env` would
# otherwise be baked into the client bundle at build time.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.local
